    "prompt": "Below is a description of the Python function `TextArea.clamp_visitable`.\n\nDescription:\n\"\"\"\nThe `clamp_visitable` function in the `TextArea` class ensures that a given location within the text area is adjusted to a position that is both valid and navigable. This is particularly useful when the cursor needs to be moved to a specific position, but that position might be out of bounds or on a line with no characters. The function takes a single parameter, `location`, which is a tuple representing the row and column of the desired position. It first attempts to retrieve the text of the specified row from the document. If the row index is out of range, it catches the `IndexError` and assigns an empty string to `line_text`. The function then clamps the row index to be within the valid range of the document's line count and the column index to be within the length of the line's text. Finally, it returns the clamped row and column as a tuple, representing the nearest visitable location. This function relies on the `clamp` helper function to restrict values to a specified range, ensuring that the cursor can only move to positions that exist within the document's content.\n\"\"\"\n\nSplit the description into atomic claims. Each claim must be a single, self-contained factual statement about the function that could be checked against the function's source code (name the function explicitly; no pronouns referring to other claims). Do not add claims that are not in the description; do not merge two facts into one claim. Keep the original wording where possible. Assign each claim exactly one type:\n- \"structural\": the function's signature, parameter names/defaults/types, return type, or which functions, methods, classes or attributes it uses.\n- \"dataflow\": how a value is computed, transformed, passed on, or what is returned for which input.\n- \"behavioural\": exceptions raised or caught, conditions/early returns, side effects, edge-case handling, ordering/iteration behaviour.\n- \"intent\": purpose, rationale, or the role of the function in the larger system.\n\nReturn a JSON array of at most 12 objects: [{\"text\": \"...\", \"type\": \"structural|dataflow|behavioural|intent\"}, ...]",
